  "label": "Anti-Asian Racism Stereotype: Driving Ability Mockery",
  "description": "This stereotype implies that Asian drivers are inherently dangerous or reckless, to the point of being memorialized after fatal accidents. It weaponizes the 'model minority' myth by mocking their perceived driving abilities, portraying them as a threat to public safety. This is a form of anti-Asian racism that contributes to prejudice and discrimination against Asian communities.",
